1. Intsall the python on server.

2. To create the python virtual env
    Run : python -m venv <name of project>
    Ex : python -m venv django_tutorial

    by that it will create the folder with django_tutorial and necessary sub folders.

3. How to login to the virtual env.
    go to created folder just click on django_tutorial --> bin --> activate (this is a file created under bin)
    Run : source <path of the actiavte file>

    In windows:
    Run : /path of activate.bat file

    So it will automaticllay login to that virtual env.

4. How to install the required modules in venv.
    Once login to the env just enter installation command like
    Run : pip install Django

5. To check the installation of modules 
    Run : python   (in venv, it will get the python terminal)
    After that run the python print statement to check the installed version

    exit()  to exit from python terminal

6.To start an project
    Run : django-admin startproject MYBlogs
    So it will create the project folder with MYBlogs under that it create th manage.py and MYBlogs folder only.

    Note : Even you run start project in any folder now you are not in venv, in that case just run that cativate file it will open the venv in yopur start project folder.

7. To start the project
